	(text "nRF52840-DK Arduino R3 headers"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d12cdcec-6e7b-5d5d-a317-892b0d08a28b")
	)
	(text "Pins assigned by symbol pin NUMBER: A4/SDA and A5/SCL are separate GPIOs on the DK.\n32 MHz lines on the only full-speed header pins: SCK P1.08 (D7), SIO0 P0.04 (A1).\nFirmware: own pinctrl for SPIM3 (not arduino_spi), high drive (H0H1) on SCK and SIO0.\nLogic runs at the DK's VDD (3.0 V as shipped): inside CO5300 IOVCC 1.65-3.3 V and VCI 2.4-3.3 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "55725e7d-0c5f-5455-a1cf-2cc14cefc7a9")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 12.7 17.78)
		(end 115.57 119.38)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "2140d83d-3b12-5f60-8f39-4e966da99c7c")
	)
	(text "Panel connector (FH26W-31S, connector pin = 32 - panel pin)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 123.19 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c977ac59-edc5-5b59-9f3f-bcb587757a0b")
	)
	(text "Silk marks PANEL PIN 1 at connector pin 31.  Bottom contact: FPC contacts face the board.\nMTP_PWR (panel 13) open; MIPI pairs (panel 23-24, 26-27, 29-30) open.\nDecoupling at the connector pins: VBAT 10u + 100n, VCI 4.7u + 100n, IOVCC 1u + 100n, TP_VDD 1u + 100n."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 123.19 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7f827ecf-b5a2-5a06-a3d8-68509401cb03")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 120.65 17.78)
		(end 289.56 154.94)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "784c9476-069f-5e18-baf6-21b894ca94f0")
	)
	(text "Panel VBAT: external source or DK VDD, through the rev B load switch"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 297.18 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7f63768f-a3f5-5ed0-b236-f80c14e1f79c")
	)
	(text "J3 takes a PPK2 in source-meter mode for the 3.0-4.5 V sweep and the current-vs-content runs.\nJ4 selects VBAT_IN: 1-2 = J3 (external), 2-3 = DK VDD (3.0 V, below the pin table's 3.7 V minimum).\nU1 is the TPS22917 rev B keeps (U21, renamed DISP_VBAT_EN): same CT and QOD wiring as rev A.\nR1 (DNP) bypasses U1 to rule it out."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 297.18 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1a43a898-e1dc-5cad-beb4-3fdd57295213")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 294.64 17.78)
		(end 447.04 87.63)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "7b21e7e2-4416-577b-a435-4ee2b24540ef")
	)
	(text "Panel logic rails from DK VDD, each separable"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 162.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d1eb7d41-e64e-5247-8ac3-87c1b9a4e656")
	)
	(text "J5 shunt carries VCI + IOVCC + TP_VDD: remove it and put a PPK2 (ammeter) across to log the logic current.\nR3-R5 split the three rails so any one can be fed or measured on its own."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 166.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f422ce89-58d3-53c2-b9d8-674acc7cb613")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 12.7 160.02)
		(end 156.21 189.23)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "8fea6bde-54cb-5037-b55a-3538f3798d0a")
	)
	(text "Display control and the 32 MHz lines"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163.83 162.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ffd5e6aa-7608-5391-8827-c5cc08290bee")
	)
	(text "R6/R7 0R at the header: swap for 22-33R if the SCK/SIO0 edges ring (CO5300 needs <= 3.5 ns 20-80 %).\nTP1-TP4 + TP5/TP6 GND beside the connector for the scope: probe at the panel end, with a spring ground.\nDISP_RES_N 1M pull-down and DISP_VCI_EN 100k pull-down hold the panel off while the DK resets.\nSIO1 (DCX) reads back on A4, a low-frequency pin: read ID/status at a reduced clock only.\nSIO2/SIO3 are unused by the single-lane driver: 10k pull-downs, TP7/TP8 for a later QSPI test."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163.83 166.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dcb0102e-9b2b-5122-ae04-8843696e74a3")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 161.29 160.02)
		(end 334.01 251.46)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "41ccb3d7-64c5-5469-be26-f9f12dfbd8d6")
	)
	(text "Touch I2C: direct at DK VDD, or level-shifted to 1.8 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 341.63 162.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2c9086e7-1d81-5160-a666-e18dcd086e21")
	)
	(text "Fitted: R14/R15 0R tie the touch bus straight to P0.26/P0.27 at 3.0 V (Waveshare runs it at 3.3 V).\n1.8 V option (the Huaxin/Viewe drawings): remove R14/R15/R16, fit U2, U3, C11, C12, R17, R18, R19.\nIn 1.8 V mode TP_INT and TP_RST_N are NOT shifted: TP_INT at 1.8 V is below the nRF's 0.7 VDD = 2.1 V\nVIH, and the nRF would drive TP_RST_N to 3.0 V.  That mode answers 'does the bus work', not 'is it done'."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 341.63 166.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "faff504e-4a68-5b1c-9694-83553ae2ef78")
	)
